      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're grieving the loss of a version of yourself that once felt strong and in control—and that grief is entirely valid. But being a passenger doesn't mean you've lost your worth; it means you're still here, enduring, which takes a different kind of courage. Purpose isn't only about action—it can also be found in how you endure, how you still notice the quiet, and how you still speak your truth. I hope you can find one small moment today where you feel like the driver again, even if it's just choosing what you look at out the window.",
